{
  "info": {
    "name": "ASIMBv API - manual QA",
    "description": "Manual QA of the ASIMBv backend. Set `baseUrl` (default http://localhost:5197) and `adminKey` (the ADMIN_API_KEY from .env; it is intentionally NOT stored in this file).\n\nAll mock data uses the reserved domain @qa-asimbv.invalid and the title \"QA MOCK EVENT\", and the run removes what it creates (the mock event via DELETE; contact messages and subscribers have no delete endpoint, so remove rows with email LIKE '%@qa-asimbv.invalid' in the database afterwards).\n\nDifferences from the original test plan, based on the code:\n- /auth/register, /auth/login and token expiry do not exist (no user accounts or JWT). Admin routes use the X-Admin-Key header, and a missing/wrong key returns 401, not 403.\n- Newsletter has no confirm step. A successful subscribe returns 200 (not 201) and a duplicate returns 409. The unsubscribe token is the only token.\nThe \"NOT IMPLEMENTED\" requests expect 404 so they start failing when those features are added, as a reminder to write real tests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
